1
00:00:03,405 --> 00:00:21,083
A bathroom vanity for Priya Patel: a 48" alcove, built from two kitchen presets.

2
00:00:21,083 --> 00:00:27,921
Start with the 36" sink base for the basin...

3
00:00:27,921 --> 00:00:34,803
...and the 18" 3-drawer base for a drawer bank beside it.

4
00:00:34,803 --> 00:00:53,783
The alcove is 48" between the walls. Set the room in the Room tab.

5
00:00:53,783 --> 00:00:56,433
Kitchen sizes don't fit: 36" + 18" is 54", 6" too wide. Click the sink base to resize it.

6
00:00:56,433 --> 00:01:04,926
Vanity sizes: 30" wide, 31-1/2" high for a comfort-height top, 21" deep.

7
00:01:04,926 --> 00:01:13,166
The drawer bank gets the same height and depth.

8
00:01:13,166 --> 00:01:17,907
Arrange again: 30" + 18" fills the 48" alcove exactly, wall to wall.

9
00:01:17,907 --> 00:01:22,231
Elevation: both boxes at 31-1/2", the basin cabinet on the left, drawers on the right.

10
00:01:22,231 --> 00:01:34,907
And in 3D.

11
00:01:34,907 --> 00:01:40,082
The Cut list: every part resized to the vanity, with edgebanding per edge.

12
00:01:40,082 --> 00:01:46,745
Hardware: Blum TANDEM 18 in slides for the drawers, Salice hinges on 3 mm plates for the doors.

13
00:01:46,745 --> 00:01:54,511
Nesting: a small job like this goes on just a few 5 x 12 ft sheets.

14
00:01:54,511 --> 00:01:57,935
The leftover board is shown as an offcut you can keep in stock for the next job.

15
00:01:57,935 --> 00:02:06,423
On the Output tab the labels and sheet maps are ready. Machine output switches stay off.

16
00:02:06,423 --> 00:02:09,424
A custom-size vanity from kitchen presets, sized to the alcove in under two minutes.
